19343399,2026-02-08,Debt collection,Other debt,Attempts to collect debt not owed,Debt is not yours,"I was contacted by Credit Collection Services , Inc. regarding an alleged debt purportedly owed to XXXX XXXX XXXX. 

The collection activity is improper, disputed, and non-compliant for the following reasons : Improper Initial Communication by Text Message Credit Collection Services initiated collection activity by text message, rather than by a proper written validation notice. A text message does not satisfy the written notice requirements of 15 U.S.C. 1692g ( a ), which requires a debt collector to provide a written notice containing specific disclosures either as the initial communication or within five ( 5 ) days thereafter.

I did not consent to receive collection communications by text message. This method of contact was unauthorized and improper.

Failure to Provide Proper Written Validation Notice To date, Credit Collection Services has failed to provide a compliant written validation notice that establishes : The amount of the alleged debt The legal basis for liability My rights to dispute and request validation Their authority to collect Collection activity commenced without first satisfying the statutory notice requirements.

Incorrect Legal Identity Used Credit Collection Services addressed this alleged debt using an incorrect and truncated name that is not my legal name. 
My correct legal name is XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX. 

Attempting to collect under an incorrect legal identity constitutes inaccurate and misleading information and raises serious concerns under 15 U.S.C. 1681e ( b ) ( failure to maintain reasonable procedures to assure maximum possible accuracy ) and 15 U.S.C. 1692e ( false or misleading representations ). 

