19363173,2026-02-09,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"I am filing this complaint because XXXX  Experian and TransUnion have continued to report inaccurate unverifiable contradictory and compromised information on my consumer credit reports despite multiple disputes and clear notice of serious reporting defects. My personal identifying information was impacted by the XXXX  data breach and the XXXX XXXX XXXX exposure which placed all credit reporting agencies on actual notice that any information associated with my identity requires heightened verification and stricter scrutiny before it can be lawfully published or maintained. Instead of applying those heightened standards the bureaus continued to rely on automated processes and furnisher responses while publishing information that is internally inconsistent impossible under Metro 2 reporting rules and incapable of verification. 

One of the primary issues involves the XXXX auto loan account. This account is being reported with a repossession status while simultaneously reflecting an active installment balance past due amounts and ongoing payment activity. These representations can not legally or logically exist at the same time under federal reporting standards. The account shows conflicting balances last activity dates and payment history across bureaus which proves the data is unreliable and not being independently verified. I previously disputed these contradictions yet the bureaus failed to correct or delete the account and continued reporting it causing ongoing harm to my credit profile. 

