19725899,2026-02-24,Debt collection,Auto debt,Attempts to collect debt not owed,Debt was already discharged in bankruptcy and is no longer owed,"I am submitting this complaint because the company continues to report and attempt to collect an alleged debt despite unresolved inaccuracies, conflicting records, and failure to provide required documentation. 
The company asserts that ample evidence has been provided to validate the alleged obligation ; however, I did not receive the documents the company claims support its position. The company has not demonstrated delivery of these materials, depriving me of the ability to review, verify, or challenge the evidence it relies upon. 
I am requesting proof of services and a complete, reconciled accounting of the alleged balance. The account history reflects that amounts were refunded, and at one point the account reflected a paid status. The company has not explained why refunds were issued, how the balance was calculated after those refunds, or how a paid status later became a delinquent balance.

The company also misrepresented my account access. I was not restricted from my account and maintained full access. I provided screenshots demonstrating this, yet the company continues to assert restricted access without addressing the contradictory evidence. 
Additionally, I was informed in or around XX/XX/year>XXXX  that the alleged debt was discharged, yet the company continues to report the account as open and delinquent to consumer reporting agencies. The company has not explained how a discharged obligation can be simultaneously reported as an active, open account. 
I further request documentation showing how the account was transferred from the dealership to the finance company, including the date of transfer, the legal basis for the transfer, and any payments, consideration, or settlement transactions exchanged between the dealership and the finance company in connection with the alleged obligation. The company has not provided proof of lawful assignment or ownership of the alleged debt. 
These contradictionsincluding refunds and paid status, alleged discharge, continued open reporting, inconsistent access claims, and lack of assignment documentationdemonstrate that the information being furnished is inaccurate, incomplete, and not supported by a reasonable investigation. 
Despite repeated notice of dispute, the company continues reporting this account without providing proof of services, a reconciled accounting, confirmation of document delivery, or documentation establishing lawful transfer and ownership. I am requesting that the CFPB review the companys conduct and require correction of inaccurate reporting and proper substantiation of any claimed obligation.",,TOYOTA MOTOR CREDIT CORPORATION,CA,92392,,Web,2026-02-24,Closed with explanation,Yes
